            0.065
          ],
          "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.09,
            0.436,
            0.109
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Know Your Contents (KYC)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.117,
            0.446,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": "? **Example 2:** Madhu and Madhav recently learnt about the importance of reading labels on processed food before purchase. They are at a shop to buy badam drink mix. They are looking at two products and wondering which has a larger share of badam. Can you figure it out? Which product uses a smaller proportion of food chemicals?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.475,
            0.117,
            0.638,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.668,
            0.108,
            0.902,
            0.295
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.338,
            0.847,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": "It is easier to compare the proportions of the ingredients if we convert them into percentages. For example,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.378,
            0.821,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": "DEF’s sugar content as a percentage of total weight $\\frac{99}{150} \\times 100 = 66\\%.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.403,
            0.845,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "? Complete this table by calculating the percentages to answer the questions:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.464,
            0.534,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "<table><tr><td></td><td></td><td>Mids</td><td>Bada</td><td>Cheddals</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><img src=\"images/page_14_table_image_8_1.jpg\"/></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_table_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.67,
            0.689,
            0.694
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Check if the percentages of each product add up to 100."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.713,
            0.549,
            0.733
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Percentage Increase or Decrease"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.74,
            0.845,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "Percentages are often used to describe the rate of change of quantities. For example,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.782,
            0.845,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": "1. Suppose the price of 1 kg tomatoes 3 years ago was ₹30, and the price now is ₹42. The increase in the price is ₹12."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.289,
            0.827,
            0.709,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} &\\text { (Percentage increases=} \\frac{a m o u n t   o f i n c r e a s e}{o r i g i n a l   a m o u n t   o r   b a s e} \\times 100 \\text {) }\\\\ &\\quad = \\frac{12}{30} \\times 100 = 40\\% .\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_14_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.897,
            0.81,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": "We say the price of tomatoes increased by 40% over the last 3 years."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.877,
